2  THE ONTOLOGY SCORE (RAR-mass space)
======================================================================================================

  conversion: M* = 1.5 x L_V(M_V) (stated M/L, G070); M_b = M* (gas-free);
  M_halo = f_dark x M_b, f_dark = 6-10 (G115/G03E).  Class boundaries in M_V:
    >1e5-class: M_V < -5.28 (f=6) / -4.73 (f=10)
    >1e6-class: M_V < -7.78 (f=6) / -7.23 (f=10)

  observed counts (raw, in-repo compendium; sky-corrected x 1/0.91):
    N_obs(>1e5 RAR) = 15-19   (corrected ~16-21)
    N_obs(>1e6 RAR) = 12      (corrected ~13)

  (a) raw score vs the committed dark-halo rows (for the record):
      class        N_obs   charge   relic5.7  relic3.3   factor(c/5.7/3.3)   sigma(c/5.7/3.3)
      >1e5 RAR        19    32076     8622     1696   x1688 / x454 / x89       7354 / 1974 / 385
      >1e6 RAR        12     4038     3927     1640   x337 / x327 / x137       1162 / 1130 / 470
      -> the galaxy counts sit 1e2-2e3x below ALL the dark-halo rows (missing-satellites
         factor), equally for both ontologies: occupation unmeasured at 1e5-1e6 (M_50 < 8.5e7,
         Nadler+20) -> the RAW counts are NOT the test (G156 C3, now a number).

  (b) the registered ratio test (occupation cancels): N_obs/c >= N_req in the class bins:
      class        N_req(5.7)  N_req(3.3)   N_obs(raw)  N_obs(corr)  at-power?
      >1e5 RAR         14.4       8.6       19       20.9      YES / YES
      >1e6 RAR      10199.2      21.8       12       13.2      no / no
      -> the 1e5-class test is AT POWER today (raw 19 >= N_req 8); the 1e6-class
         needs 10199 counts (x38 the full-sky census): not a census bin (committed G156 C7).

  (c) the measured suppression at the 1e5-class (charge anchors the LF):
      S_meas = 1.0 (no break) vs relic5.7 S = 0.269 (3.2 sigma) / relic3.3 S = 0.053 (4.1 sigma)
