         relic's truncated prediction 5 (5.7 keV) / 1 (3.3 keV) objects at the class.

======================================================================================================
3  THE NEXT-CENSUS REGISTRY (Rubin era)
======================================================================================================

  Rubin-era census adds: completeness to the M_V ~ 0-class at D_GC <= 300 kpc over ~100% of the
  high-lat sky (LSST r ~ 27.5; DELVE full: corrected total 265^(+79,-47) for M_V <= 0).
  Discovery potential: 200 objects above M_V = 0 (265 total - 65 confirmed) -- the LF is still
  completeness-limited ~4x at the faint end (the DES Y3 census's 'no new candidates at depth'
  shows the yield is the completeness correction, not new bright objects).

  Sample size that flips the verdict (registered rule, G156 C8):
    1e5-class: N_req = 8.6 (3.3 keV) / 14.4 (5.7 keV) -> ALREADY REACHED (raw 19, corr ~21):
              the lower-edge verdict flip is ARMED; the Rubin census runs it at ~3-4x power.
    1e6-class: N_req = 21.8 (3.3 keV) / 10199 (5.7 keV) = x38.5 the census -> the census CANNOT
              flip it; the window decision is the dark-halo slope probes' (lensing >= 100 quads,
              >= 5 streams at Rubin depth -- G156 V3).  The census verdict CONVERGES at the lower
              edge by the Rubin era.

