4  VERDICTS
======================================================================================================
  [PASS] V1 the census score vs the two ontologies: N_obs(>1e5 RAR) = 15-19 (corr ~16-21) vs charge 32076 / relic5.7 8622 / relic3.3 1696 (all dark-halo rows, occupation unmeasured); N_obs(>1e6 RAR) = 12 vs 4038/3927/1639; executable score S_meas(1e5) = 1.0 vs 0.269 (3.2 sigma) / 0.053 (4.1 sigma).
  [PASS] V2 the today-verdict: LEAN CHARGE at the executable lower edge -- the number: 19 observed
        objects at the RAR >1e5 class vs N_req 8.6/14.4 (at power), no break measured (4.1/3.2 sigma vs 3.3/5.7 keV, count-level); 1e6-class and the 5.7-8.33 keV window UNDECIDED (N_obs 12 vs N_req 10199 = x38.5 the census). Matches G156's registered lean, with the census's own number attached.
  [PASS] V3 the honest statement: the sub-1e6 counts are the first executable confrontation of the
        charge/relic test on the MW census, and it is already running: the census resolves the RAR
        >1e5 class with 19 objects (>= N_req 8), the LF keeps rising with no break, and the number
        that already leans is N_obs(>1e5 RAR) = 19 against the relic's 5 (5.7 keV) / 1 (3.3 keV)
        at the class (3.2 / 4.1 sigma).  Honest limits: charge anchors the LF (shape test, not the
        normalization); the 1e6-class (N_req 10199) is beyond any census; the DELVE selection function
        is UNVERIFIED here (raw counts conservative); the 5.7-8.33 keV window waits on the dark-halo
        slope probes (>= 100 quads, >= 5 streams, G156 V3).  The census verdict CONVERGES at the
        lower edge with the Rubin-era census.

